The changelog system tracks application changes through a multi-stage pipeline that integrates GitHub releases, commit analysis, and AI-powered categorization:

**1. GitHub Release Sync** (changelog-sync.service.ts:71-85, 106-127): A scheduled cron job runs every 6 hours to fetch releases from the GitHub API and detect which parts of the codebase changed:

```typescript
@Cron(CronExpression.EVERY_6_HOURS)
async scheduledSync() {
  const releases = await this.fetchReleases();
  for (const release of releases) {
    const commits = await this.fetchCommitsForRelease(release, releases);
    const { hasBackend, hasFrontend } = this.detectChangeAreas(commits);
    await this.changelogService.upsertEntry({
      tagName: release.tag_name,
      rawCommits: commits as unknown as Prisma.JsonArray,
      hasBackendChanges: hasBackend,
      hasFrontendChanges: hasFrontend,
      isPrerelease: release.prerelease,
    });
  }
}
```

**2. Change Area Detection** (changelog-sync.service.ts:284-336): Analyzes commit messages using regex patterns to classify changes as backend (service.ts, controller.ts, resolver.ts, database, apps/whk-wms/) or frontend (component, react, .tsx, apps/whk-wms-front-end/):

```typescript
private detectChangeAreas(commits: GitHubCommit[]) {
  const backendPatterns = [/\bbackend\b/i, /\.service\.ts/i, /\.controller\.ts/i, ...];
  const frontendPatterns = [/\bfrontend\b/i, /\.tsx$/i, /\breact\b/i, ...];
  for (const commit of commits) {
    if (backendPatterns.some((pattern) => pattern.test(commit.commit.message))) {
      hasBackend = true;
    }
    if (frontendPatterns.some((pattern) => pattern.test(commit.commit.message))) {
      hasFrontend = true;
    }
  }
}
```

